lines+=['','The later-period new runner averages12.9 simulated entries/day. Of258 markets, **133 were absent from the one-contract current-design portfolio**, while125 overlapped. They are not258 additional opportunities. Combining both designs with one contract each and shared one-market-per-asset limits produced394 trades, versus261 for the current design, a50.96% increase; modeled net was+$16.3310 versus+$13.3508. This equal-size comparison is not the actual five-contract operating setup.','','The two lane totals are not simply added: duplicate markets and entry timing affect which lane gets a position. September standalone lane checks were145/145 wins for strong cushion (+$3.1119) and141 trades/127 wins/14 losses for value (+$5.5929), before resolving cross-lane overlap. The combined runner had258 trades/244 wins/14 losses and+$7.8967.','','## Interaction with the actual five-contract sizing','','A shared-budget replay with current5ct plus experimental1ct, under the then-active8/$7.60/$10 limits (subsequently raised to20/$19/$10), produced362 trades and+$47.4054, versus200 trades and+$51.1662 for current5ct alone. The experimental lane contributed+$5.6808, but it occupied markets/capacity that otherwise admitted larger current-design positions. Current-design fills dropped from200 to175 (31 old markets displaced, six different current-design markets added). More tickets therefore did not improve this combination.','','**The deployed experiment has a completely separate virtual ledger and cannot consume live funds, capacity, or market slots.** Any later real-money combination needs a shared risk/ownership coordinator, explicit allocation, and another interaction replay. Merely launching two independent order writers is not a completed design.','','## Robustness and what remains unproven','','September pair sensitivities: +$6.0023 when charging every accepted fill at its permitted cap, +$6.8000 with whole-cent debit rounding, +$5.3167 with2c stress, and +$3.3317 with an additional full-minute quote delay. The latter delay exceeds the real35-second freshness rule and is a sensitivity only, not a proposed execution path. Delayed quotes charged at the original cap lose$0.8006.','','The older August13–27 recorded-book sample loses$1.2320 when charged entirely at the permitted cap despite a positive displayed-price result. Removing its best three days also makes the result negative. The September portfolio remains+$3.8575 after removing its three best days, but this does not fix selection bias.','','A day-block bootstrap on September gives an unadjusted95% EV interval of+0.3893 to+5.4584c/contract. Correcting the one-sided lower tail for the12 inspected candidates gives**−0.6948c**, so this study does not establish a statistically reliable positive edge. Same-day crypto correlation is grouped by day; longer regime dependence can still be underestimated. The strong-cushion lane’s zero recent losses is a small-sample observation, not a zero-loss property.','','The rule list was frozen before this screen. However, the two selected lanes and their combination were chosen after seeing the retrospective results, and these historical dates have been examined in previous studies. The `fit`, `selection`, and `later` labels describe chronology; they are not a claim of pristine untouched holdouts for this final combined candidate. Fresh frozen forward data is the next test.','','## All12 candidates, including failures','','This screen is one first accepted entry per market, before the separate portfolio allocator. Each cell is trade count / net at one contract after fees and1c stress; all later-period rows exclude October2.','','| Rule | Aug28–Sep11 quote | Aug28–Sep11 books | Sep12–Oct1 quote |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
