lines+=['','Late z2/z3 entries and early entries did not survive all execution checks. The wider Gaussian5c rule had more trades but only+$0.3717 at cap cost across the20 full later days; its initial screen including the partial October2 day was negative at cap cost; the broad z2 rule lost in the selection quote period. The empirical probability fit failed its delayed later-period check. The premiumz2.5 rule had weaker old-period and delay results than premiumz3. These failures are retained rather than hidden by the chosen pair.','','## Data, execution and validation','','- Public Kalshi market metadata/outcomes/candles and Coinbase completed-minute histories were reconstructed from raw inputs; no old ledger-z filtering.19,000 records in the initial pull,18,936 in the primary50-day window; recurring absent markets are not fabricated.717 minute observations in the initial screen lack full spot history and are rejected.','- The older cache provides315,432 recorded book snapshots across11,352 markets. A book must follow the decision by0.3–35s and display full intended quantity inside its tick-rounded cap. Missing or stale books do not receive synthetic fills. The historical screen uses the first available subsequent snapshot per qualifying minute; the forward runner can recheck rejected books within25s, up to8 checks, with35s final deadline. The replay does not award extra hypothetical retry fills.','- Book liquidity is an observation, not proof that an IOC would have filled. September has price-only proxies; no September historical depth is invented. The next minute opening quote may be carried forward and lacks a precise subsecond timestamp. Historical Coinbase data can be revised; the forward runner saves the actual completed bars it saw.','- The full-minute delayed screen preserves the original score to measure sensitivity. The forward bot never intentionally trades signals that old.','- Fee model:7% × quantity × price ×(1−price), aligned debit rounded to$0.0001; whole-cent rounding tested separately. This follows the [Kalshi fee schedule](https://kalshi.com/docs/kalshi-fee-schedule.pdf) and [fee-rounding documentation](https://docs.kalshi.com/getting_started/fee_rounding). It is not a reconstruction of actual historical fragmented-fill rebates. [Candlestick documentation](https://docs.kalshi.com/api-reference/market/get-market-candlesticks) describes the quote fields, not a guarantee of available quantity.','- The independent capacity replay reproduced the prior full-engine September23–October1 control exactly:71 trades,70W/1L,+$21.1726 before stress, and+$18.7443 at cap cost.','-15 research/paper tests passed, including300 sampled comparisons with the active scanner, future-bar exclusion, complete volatility history, signal boundaries, YES/NO tick rounding, full depth, fee rounding, timing, duplicate persistence across restart, risk reservation, simulated entry and idempotent settlement. All test sockets are blocked. Six additional capacity-proposal tests passed.','- Historical drawdown here groups P&L by market close; it is not intratrade mark-to-market drawdown or a worst possible loss.','','## Running state and next evidence','','Server directory: `/home/varma/kalshi_parallel_design_2026_10_02`. Enabled user service: `kalshi-parallel-research.service`. Local source and evidence live in this research folder. `paper_state/status.json` reports freshness, lanes, rejections, entries, wins/losses, open simulations and stressed net. `paper_state/paper.sqlite3` retains original signal/book observations and paper entries. This is a persistent server program, not a scheduled Codex follow-up.','','The runner has no credentials, account endpoints, order submission code or live mode. It makes allowlisted public GET requests only. Source hashes and selected rules are frozen in `paper_config.json`; an unexpected source change prevents startup. It automatically records future public settlements in its own ledger. The observed startup scanned all four live markets successfully; no paper entries had occurred at the deployment verification snapshot.','','The forward review target is at least28 calendar days and200 settled distinct markets under unchanged parameters, followed by costs, depth, clustered-loss, and aggregate-allocation checks. No automatic promotion or real-money activation is configured. Reaching a trade count alone is insufficient.','','Production code and the September28 stable checkpoint are hash-checked unchanged. The current five-contract bot remains live and armed. Only the isolated paper service was enabled in this work.','','## Reproduce and files','','```sh','python3 kalshi_parallel_design_2026_10_02/research.py --rebuild','python3 kalshi_parallel_design_2026_10_02/portfolio.py','python3 kalshi_parallel_design_2026_10_02/test_research.py','```','','`rules.json` records the pre-screen12-rule list; `PLAN.json` records scope; `coverage.json` hashes the inputs; `screen.json` preserves all outcomes; `portfolio_results.json`/`portfolio_trades.json` contain full portfolio metrics and trades; `mixed_size_interaction.json` preserves the actual-size collision test; `portfolio_control.json` verifies the prior engine control; `tests.log` records validation; `production_before.json` and `verification.json` record live-source preservation. `capacity_candidate/` is a review-only proposal, not a deployment.']
